Description: Fix CVE-2026-3505 — reject out-of-range / unsupported PGP AEAD (OCB) packets at the packet-dispatch boundary to prevent pre-authentication resource exhaustion (CWE-770 / RFC 9580 5.13.2).
 bcpg-jdk15on 1.64 has no AEAD Encrypted Data Packet parser (tag 20); an AEAD
 packet therefore falls through BCPGInputStream.readPacket() to the generic
 "unknown packet type" default. This defensive change names the AEAD packet tag
 and rejects it explicitly with a clear, deterministic error before any
 attacker-controlled chunk-size octet in the packet body can be consumed by a
 (present or back-ported) AEAD handler. This guarantees the vulnerable
 out-of-range chunk-size code path can never be reached in this artifact,
 mirroring the upstream RFC 9580 5.13.2 chunk-size range check.
Origin: ai-synthesized, CVE-2026-3505
Author: Root.io Novel Patcher <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-08-23
